{%- comment -%}
  PG R36S Ultra Cart (2026-09-23): cloned from sections/pg-pro2-cart.liquid
  for the Pocket Era R36S Ultra (pocket-era-r36s-ultra), which has the same
  option shape (Bundle / Color). Without it pg-cart-variants puts its generic
  picker on Ultra lines, labelled by colour only, where a pick can swap a Max
  Bundle for a Single. Changed: HANDLE, window flag pgUltraCart, the CSS
  href, the TITLE map, the schema name, and the picker marker, which is
  data-pg-ul / dataset.pgUl in the lookup, the read AND the build (renaming
  only the lookup made the R36H clone's picker flicker, pg-r36h-cart.liquid
  2026-09-22). The notes below came over with the code, reworded for the Ultra.

  From the Pro 2 file (2026-09-16, swap rewritten 2026-09-17): the bundle
  lines in the cart drawer and on the cart page read like the R36S pack lines.

  THE PROBLEM. The Ultra carries every offer as one variant of one product
  with TWO options (Bundle / Color). pg-cart-variants builds an in-cart picker
  for any multi-variant line and labels each option with the LAST segment of
  the variant title, so a Max Bundle line would read "Pocket Era R36S Ultra"
  over a picker that said "White" and opened onto each colour twice (once per
  tier) -- and choosing one could silently swap a $139.99 Max Bundle for a
  $109.99 Single.

  THE FIX, per line of this product:
    - the title names the tier the way the pack lines do ("Pocket Era R36S
      Duo Pack"): "R36S Ultra Max Bundle", or the product title for the
      single (a Duo Max is two Max consoles; its TITLE key is kept from the Pro 2
      map and matches no Ultra variant today);
    - the picker is rebuilt from the variants of the SAME tier only, labelled
      by colour ("Transparent Blue"), so a shopper can change colours in the
      cart but never the tier or the price;
    - it wears pg-cart-variants' own .pg-vsel class, so that section styles it
      with arm() and, seeing a picker already on the line, does not build its
      own over it. Ours is marked data-pg-ul so it is never mistaken for theirs.

  THE SWAP IS ONE WRITE NOW, AND THE PICTURE CHANGES AT ONCE (2026-09-17, by
  report: "when they switch color it should change quick, the cart was taking
  way too long"). The first cut read /cart.js, removed the old line, added the
  new one and then refreshed the drawer: three requests in a row before the
  refresh even started, and the old colour's photo on screen the whole time.
    - /cart/update.js takes the old variant to 0 and the new one to the line's
      quantity in a SINGLE request (it adds a variant the cart does not hold),
      so the cart is never empty in between and two round trips are gone. The
      quantities are read off the rendered lines, not from /cart.js. If the
      new colour is already in the cart as its own line, its quantity is
      added to, not overwritten.
    - the line's photo is switched to the picked colour the instant the picker
      changes, from the variant images in the product JSON, and the colour
      photos are preloaded as soon as an Ultra line is seen, so the change is
      on screen before the request leaves.
  The drawer refresh that follows is pg-drawer's, unchanged.

  A TAP ON THE PICKER WENT TO THE TITLE (2026-09-17, by report from an iPhone:
  "I'm clicking the color button in cart and it thinks I'm clicking the
  title"). The picker was 32px tall and sits a few pixels under the product
  title, which is a link, and the row's link is also what a tap falls through
  to whenever the picker's paragraph is not marked clickable (pg-drawer's
  section > p:not(.pg-varp){pointer-events:none}). Three changes, phone only
  (760px, the width pg-cart-imglink uses for its picture tap):
    - on a line that has a picker, the TITLE is no longer a link. The picture
      still opens the product (pg-cart-imglink reads the row's href, which
      pointer-events does not touch), so nothing is lost and a near miss on the
      picker can no longer leave the cart. This is a CSS rule on any line with
      a .pg-vsel, so the size pickers on the other products get it too;
    - the Ultra picker is 40px tall, the smallest comfortable thumb target,
      with 6px of air between it and the title. pg-cart-variants' arm() stamps
      32px inline once, so the height is stamped after it has run;
    - the picker's paragraph is re-marked clickable on EVERY pass, not only on
      the pass that builds the select, so it cannot be left inert.

  A COLOUR CHANGE DOES NOT FLASH (2026-09-17, by report: "when they switch
  color in the cart there shouldn't be a flash"). Measured on the draft: the
  write takes about 0.65s, the list dims to 55% while it is in flight
  (pg-cart-smooth) and comes back; the drawer then swaps the row for the
  server's bare one, whose picture is a NEW <img> at a different URL (not
  loaded yet: blank), whose title is the product's again and whose picker is
  plain text, and the picker only came back 50 to 140ms later, unstyled at
  first, fading in, 6px lower. The picker also went grey (disabled) for the
  whole write. Now, for a colour change on this product only:
    - #cart carries data-pg-quiet for the length of the swap: no dimming and
      no fade-in (the list still takes no taps while the write is in flight);
    - the picker is not disabled, it just stops taking taps;
    - the row is dressed again in the SAME task as the drawer's swap (the
      MutationObserver runs pass() at once while a swap is on, before the
      browser paints), and the new picker starts with the old one's inline
      styles, so pg-cart-variants' later arm() changes nothing on screen;
    - the old row's <img>, already showing the new colour from cache, is moved
      into the new row in place of the server's unloaded one;
    - the height ease pg-cart-smooth starts for the 6px it saw missing is
      cleared, because nothing is missing any more.

  Runs on the drawer's rebuild beat (pg:cart-updated, a MutationObserver on
  #cart, and a 400ms tick) because the drawer replaces its rows on every cart
  change. Registered in sections/header-group.json.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  @media (max-width:760px){
    #cart .l4ca > li:has(select.pg-vsel) h2 a,
    #cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-pick] h2 a,
    body.template-cart .form-cart .l4ca > li:has(select.pg-vsel) h2 a,
    body.template-cart .form-cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-pick] h2 a{pointer-events:none !important;cursor:default}
    #cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-pick] section > p.pg-varp{margin-top:6px !important}
    /* pg-cart-smooth holds 32px for a picker that is being rebuilt; this one is 40 */
    #cart .l4ca > li[data-pg-hadsel]:has(a[href*="/products/pocket-era-r36s-ultra"]) section > p{min-height:40px}
  }
  /* a colour change is quiet: no dimming while the write is in flight */
  #cart#cart[data-pg-quiet] .l4ca:not(.in-panel),
  #cart#cart[data-pg-quiet] .l4tt{opacity:1 !important;transition:none !important}
  #cart#cart[data-pg-quiet] .l4ca .pg-vsel,
  #cart#cart[data-pg-quiet] .l4ca > li[data-pg-new]{animation:none !important}
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgUltraCart) return; window.pgUltraCart = 1;

  var HANDLE = 'pocket-era-r36s-ultra';
  var TITLE = {
    'Single Device (64GB)': 'Pocket Era R36S Ultra',
    'Max Bundle (128GB)': 'R36S Ultra Max Bundle',
    'Duo Max Bundle (2x 128GB)': 'R36S Ultra Duo Max Bundle'
  };
  var LINES = '#cart .l4ca:not(.in-panel) > li, body.template-cart .form-cart .l4ca:not(.in-panel) > li';

  var VARS = null, loading = false, warmed = false;
  function load(){
    if (VARS || loading) return;
    loading = true;
    fetch('/products/' + HANDLE + '.js')
      .then(function(r){ return r.json(); })
      .then(function(p){ VARS = (p && p.variants) || []; })
      .catch(function(){ loading = false; });
  }
  function byId(id){
    for (var i = 0; i < VARS.length; i++){ if (String(VARS[i].id) === String(id)) return VARS[i]; }
    return null;
  }
  function label(v){
    return v.option3 && v.option3 !== 'None' ? (v.option2 + ' + ' + v.option3) : v.option2;
  }
  function photoOf(v){
    var src = v && v.featured_image && v.featured_image.src;
    if (!src) return '';
    src = String(src);
    return src + (src.indexOf('?') > -1 ? '&' : '?') + 'width=360';
  }
  /* the colour photos, fetched once so a switch paints from cache */
  function warm(){
    if (warmed || !VARS) return;
    warmed = true;
    var seen = {};
    VARS.forEach(function(v){
      var u = photoOf(v);
      if (!u || seen[u]) return;
      seen[u] = 1;
      var im = new Image(); im.decoding = 'async'; im.src = u;
    });
  }
  function showPhoto(li, v){
    var u = photoOf(v);
    if (!u) return;
    var img = li.querySelector('figure img, picture img, img');
    if (!img) return;
    var pic = img.closest('picture');
    if (pic) pic.querySelectorAll('source').forEach(function(s){ s.setAttribute('srcset', u); });
    img.removeAttribute('srcset');
    img.removeAttribute('sizes');
    img.setAttribute('src', u);
  }

  /* While a swap is in flight the line is stamped as the NEW variant. Every
     watcher in the drawer reads a line's variant off its product link, and
     pg-cart-addons re-checks each line's photo against what /cart.js holds for
     that variant about once a second: left pointing at the old variant, the
     old colour's photo would be put straight back over the new one. */
  function pointAt(li, vid){
    Array.prototype.forEach.call(li.querySelectorAll('a[href*="variant="]'), function(a){
      var h = a.getAttribute('href') || '';
      a.setAttribute('href', h.replace(/([?&]variant=)\d+/, '$1' + vid));
    });
  }

  function lineInfo(li){
    if (li.closest('.nc-recs, .nc-recs-panel, .pg-unlock')) return null;
    var a = li.querySelector('h2 a[href*="/products/' + HANDLE + '"], a[href*="/products/' + HANDLE + '"]');
    if (!a) return null;
    var m = (a.getAttribute('href') || '').match(/[?&]variant=(\d+)/);
    if (!m) return null;
    return {a: a, vid: m[1]};
  }
  function qtyOf(li){
    var input = li.querySelector('.semantic-amount input, .input-amount input, input[type=number]');
    return input ? (parseInt(input.value, 10) || 0) : 0;
  }

  /* the <p> holding the variant text or a picker someone else built */
  function pickerSlot(li){
    var sel = li.querySelector('select.pg-vsel');
    if (sel && sel.parentElement) return sel.parentElement;
    var ps = li.querySelectorAll('section p, p');
    for (var i = 0; i < ps.length; i++){
      var t = (ps[i].textContent || '').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
      if (/Bundle|Single Device/.test(t) && /\//.test(t)) return ps[i];
    }
    return null;
  }

  /* the row belongs to the picker: marked on every pass, because the mark is
     what makes the paragraph take taps at all */
  function claim(li, slot){
    if (!li.hasAttribute('data-pg-pick')) li.setAttribute('data-pg-pick', '1');
    if (!slot.classList.contains('pg-varp')) slot.classList.add('pg-varp');
    if (slot.style.getPropertyValue('pointer-events') !== 'auto'){
      slot.style.setProperty('pointer-events', 'auto', 'important');
      slot.style.setProperty('position', 'relative', 'important');
      slot.style.setProperty('z-index', '6', 'important');
    }
  }
  /* a thumb-sized target on a phone. Waits for pg-cart-variants' arm() (it
     stamps height:32px inline, once) so this lands after it and stays. */
  var PHONE = window.matchMedia ? window.matchMedia('(max-width:760px)') : null;
  function roomy(sel){
    if (!sel || !sel.dataset.pgVar || sel.dataset.pgRoomy) return;
    if (!PHONE || !PHONE.matches) return;
    sel.dataset.pgRoomy = '1';
    sel.style.setProperty('height', '40px', 'important');
    sel.style.setProperty('min-height', '40px', 'important');
  }

  /* what a colour change carries across the drawer's row swap */
  var CARRY = null, quietTimer = null;
  function quiet(on){
    var c = document.getElementById('cart');
    if (quietTimer){ clearTimeout(quietTimer); quietTimer = null; }
    if (!c) return;
    if (on){
      c.setAttribute('data-pg-quiet', '1');
      /* never left on: a write that hangs must not leave the cart undimmable */
      quietTimer = setTimeout(function(){ quiet(false); }, 7000);
    } else {
      c.removeAttribute('data-pg-quiet');
      CARRY = null;
    }
  }
  /* the row the drawer just put in, made to look like the one it replaced */
  function settle(li, slot, sel){
    if (!CARRY) return;
    if (CARRY.selCss){
      sel.style.cssText = CARRY.selCss;
      /* it wears pg-cart-variants' styles already, and this file's 40px: marked
         as done, so neither arm() (32px, then 40 again a pass later) nor
         roomy() touches it. refit() still re-measures it on a resize. */
      if (CARRY.armed){
        sel.dataset.pgVar = '1';
        if (CARRY.fitW) sel.dataset.pgFitW = CARRY.fitW;
        if (CARRY.roomy) sel.dataset.pgRoomy = '1';
      }
    }
    sel.style.setProperty('animation', 'none', 'important');
    sel.style.removeProperty('pointer-events');
    if (CARRY.slotCss) slot.style.cssText = CARRY.slotCss;
    var img = li.querySelector('figure img, picture img, img');
    var old = CARRY.img;
    if (old && img && old !== img && img.parentNode && !old.isConnected){
      old.setAttribute('alt', img.getAttribute('alt') || '');
      img.parentNode.replaceChild(old, img);
    }
    var list = li.parentNode;
    if (list && list.style){
      list.style.height = ''; list.style.overflow = ''; list.style.transition = '';
    }
  }

  var busy = false;
  function swap(oldVid, newId, li, sel){
    if (busy) return;
    busy = true;
    var q = qtyOf(li) || 1;
    /* the picked colour may already be a line of its own: add to it */
    var already = 0;
    Array.prototype.forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll(LINES), function(other){
      if (other === li) return;
      var info = lineInfo(other);
      if (info && String(info.vid) === String(newId)) already += (qtyOf(other) || 1);
    });
    var updates = {};
    updates[String(oldVid)] = 0;
    updates[String(newId)] = already + q;
    fetch('/cart/update.js', {
      method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'}, credentials: 'same-origin',
      body: JSON.stringify({updates: updates})
    }).then(function(r){
      if (!r || !r.ok) throw new Error('update');
      busy = false;
      if (window.pgDrawerRefresh) return window.pgDrawerRefresh();
      window.location.reload();
    }).then(function(){
      /* a moment for the other sections' own passes, then the cart dims and
         fades as usual again */
      if (quietTimer) clearTimeout(quietTimer);
      quietTimer = setTimeout(function(){ quiet(false); }, 1200);
    }).catch(function(){
      /* sold out in that colour, or the write failed: put the line back the
         way it was and let the drawer confirm it */
      busy = false;
      quiet(false);
      li.removeAttribute('data-pg-swapping');
      pointAt(li, oldVid);
      var old = VARS && byId(oldVid);
      if (old) showPhoto(li, old);
      if (sel){ sel.value = String(oldVid); sel.style.removeProperty('pointer-events'); }
      if (window.pgDrawerRefresh){ try { window.pgDrawerRefresh(); } catch (e){} }
    });
  }

  function dress(li){
    if (li.hasAttribute('data-pg-swapping')) return;   /* mid-swap: leave the line alone */
    var info = lineInfo(li);
    if (!info) return;
    var v = byId(info.vid);
    if (!v) return;

    /* the tier in the title, like "Pocket Era R36S Duo Pack" */
    var want = TITLE[v.option1] || info.a.textContent.trim();
    if (info.a.textContent.trim() !== want) info.a.textContent = want;

    /* the colour picker, scoped to this tier */
    var slot = pickerSlot(li);
    if (!slot) return;
    claim(li, slot);
    var mine = slot.querySelector('select[data-pg-ul]');
    if (mine && mine.dataset.pgUl === info.vid){ roomy(mine); return; }   /* built for this line already */

    var sel = document.createElement('select');
    sel.className = 'pg-vsel';
    sel.dataset.pgUl = info.vid;   /* data-pg-ul: the attribute the lookup above finds */
    sel.setAttribute('aria-label', v.option3 && v.option3 !== 'None' ? 'Console colors' : 'Color');
    VARS.forEach(function(x){
      if (x.option1 !== v.option1) return;
      if (x.available === false && String(x.id) !== String(v.id)) return;
      var o = document.createElement('option');
      o.value = x.id;
      o.textContent = label(x);
      if (String(x.id) === String(v.id)) o.selected = true;
      sel.appendChild(o);
    });
    sel.addEventListener('change', function(){
      var id = sel.value;
      if (!id || String(id) === String(v.id)) return;
      /* the new colour's photo first, then the write */
      var nv = byId(id);
      li.setAttribute('data-pg-swapping', '1');
      pointAt(li, id);
      if (nv) showPhoto(li, nv);
      /* not disabled (a disabled picker turns grey for the whole write): it
         just stops taking taps until the row is replaced */
      CARRY = {vid: String(id), img: li.querySelector('figure img, picture img, img'), selCss: sel.style.cssText, slotCss: slot.style.cssText,
        armed: !!sel.dataset.pgVar, fitW: sel.dataset.pgFitW || '', roomy: !!sel.dataset.pgRoomy};
      sel.style.setProperty('pointer-events', 'none', 'important');
      quiet(true);
      swap(v.id, id, li, sel);
    });
    ['click', 'mousedown', 'touchstart', 'pointerdown'].forEach(function(ev){
      sel.addEventListener(ev, function(e){ e.stopPropagation(); }, true);
    });
    slot.textContent = '';
    slot.appendChild(sel);
    claim(li, slot);
    if (CARRY && CARRY.vid === String(info.vid)) settle(li, slot, sel);
    /* pg-cart-variants' arm() styles every .pg-vsel on its own mutation beat;
       roomy() follows it on the next pass here */
  }

  function pass(){
    var lis = document.querySelectorAll(LINES);
    if (!lis.length) return;
    var any = false;
    for (var i = 0; i < lis.length; i++){ if (lineInfo(lis[i])){ any = true; break; } }
    if (!any) return;
    if (!VARS){ load(); return; }
    warm();
    Array.prototype.forEach.call(lis, function(li){ try { dress(li); } catch (e){} });
  }

  setInterval(pass, 400);
  document.addEventListener('pg:cart-updated', function(){ try { pass(); } catch (e){} });
  (function watchCart(){
    var c = document.getElementById('cart');
    if (!c || !window.MutationObserver){ setTimeout(watchCart, 500); return; }
    var queued = false;
    new MutationObserver(function(){
      /* mid colour change: dress the new row NOW, in the same task as the
         drawer's swap, so it is never painted bare */
      if (CARRY){ try { pass(); } catch (e){} return; }
      if (queued) return;
      queued = true;
      setTimeout(function(){ queued = false; pass(); }, 0);
    }).observe(c, {childList: true, subtree: true});
  })();
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', pass); else pass();
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG R36S Ultra Cart", "settings": [], "presets": [{"name": "PG R36S Ultra Cart"}]}
{% endschema %}
